                <pb facs="0350" n="226" sameAs="frus:frus1921v01/pg226"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">718.1915/565a: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Minister in Panama</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Price</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1921-08-25T18:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">August 25,
                                1921—6 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>66. Please notify Panaman Government that Costa Rican Legation here has been
                    instructed to inform Department that Costa Rican Government intends assuming
                    jurisdiction on September 5th, over <pb facs="0351" n="227" xml:id="pg227"/>
                    that portion of the territory in the region of the Pacific awarded to Costa Rica
                    by the terms of the Loubet Award, which has hitherto been occupied by the
                    Government of Panama.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hughes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
